iabetic complication (e.g., retinopathy): contradicted by acute visual changes and nonfocal neurological findings", "Metabolic/endocrine syndrome: serum electrolytes and glucose are normal despite diabetes history", "Paraneoplastic neurological syndrome: possible but less supported than direct hematologic malignancy given lab findings"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blasts (suggestive of hematologic malignancy)", "Acute visual changes (20/100 acuity in both eyes)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4726947179946284, "posterior": 0.08519340969424441, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The high blast percentage and pancytopenia are inconsistent with multiple myeloma, which does not involve blasts in peripheral blood."], "evidence_against": ["Acute visual changes are not typical for myeloid neoplasms, mildly reducing their likelihood but not excluding blast crisis or other sub-entities."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.15666965085049236, "posterior": 0.31113182825417285, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The lack of confirmed lymphoid lineage markers reduces support for lymphoid neoplasms (B2) compared to myeloid differentials."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [],