irst:  abdominal pain, abnormal/excessive bleeding, anemia, confusion, easy bruising\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, bleeding easily, blurred vision, enlarged spleen, feeling full after eating small amounts\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis (CML-BC) vs Plasma Cell Myeloma (Multiple Myeloma):\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n  Favours second: abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, decreased circulating antibody level, elevated serum creatinine\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis (CML-BC) vs Waldenström Macroglobulinemia:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n\nDe Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) vs Lymphoblastic Lymphoma with Leukemic Phase:\n  Favours first:  balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, bone pain, enlarged liver\n\nDe Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Chronic/Accelerated Phase:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, cellular immunodeficiency, chronic lymphatic leukemia\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n\nDe Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) vs Plasma Cell Myeloma (Multiple Myeloma):"}
